steps.detail:
Vomiting can be a sign of other emergencies that have their own protocols:
- a recent head injury: vomiting is a danger sign;
- an injury to the belly;
- a possible poison (MedlinePlus: call 911 if you think vomiting is from poisoning);
- carbon monoxide: headache, nausea or vomiting, often several people in a tent, cabin or vehicle with a stove, heater or engine;
- heat illness after exertion or in hot weather.

Several people ill at the same time can mean a shared poison, fumes, or contaminated food or water (Red Cross Poison Exposure marks multiple people affected as needing immediate emergency care).
